Project: DayZero - Windows setup toolkit on a USB stick.
- builder\  : USB Builder (PowerShell 5.1 + WPF). Builder.ps1 + Builder.xaml. Makes the Windows USB stick (lib\WinMedia.psm1: download from Microsoft or ISO, diskpart, DISM), writes autounattend.xml and copies kit\ to the stick.
- kit\      : runs on the new PC. DayZero.ps1 = wizard. kit\lib\*.psm1 = modules (order in Modules.ps1).
- kit\config\*.json : modes, apps (winget IDs), tweaks, debloat levels, drivers, office. Most changes are JSON only.
- kit\lang\ru.json : Russian texts as pairs [English shown text, translation]. kit\lib\Lang.psm1 translates where text is shown (Get-DzText). Add a pair for every new text shown to the user; tests\Lang.Tests.ps1 fails otherwise. Logs stay English.
- kit\ui\Theme.xaml : all colours/styles (monochrome). Keep resource key names (DzMagenta etc.), code uses them.
- builder\lib\Linux.psm1 + builder\linux\*.json : Linux install sticks (Ubuntu autoinstall, ISO download + SHA-256, Windows->Linux locale/keyboard/time zone maps).
- builder\LinuxPanel.xaml + LinuxBuilder.ps1 : the LINUX side of the builder window, shown by the WINDOWS | LINUX switch in the header (dot-sourced by Builder.ps1). builder\lib\RawWrite.psm1 : any ISO byte for byte + read-back.
- build-dayzero-usb.sh + builder\BuilderCli.ps1 + builder\lib\LinuxHost.psm1 : the builder on Linux (PowerShell 7 only; may use PS7/.NET 6 APIs with a SuppressMessage that says why).
- kit\linux\ : Linux first-boot setup (dayzero.py, Python 3 stdlib only), installed to /opt/dayzero by install-kit.sh. Apps in kit\linux\apps.json (Flathub ids). Your scripts: kit\Scripts-Linux\*.sh.
- tests\    : Pester tests. Run: pwsh tools\Invoke-DzChecks.ps1 (tests + PSScriptAnalyzer). Must stay green.

Hard rules:
- .ps1/.psm1 files must be plain ASCII (PowerShell 5.1). .cmd files keep CRLF.
- autounattend.xml must never select, wipe or partition a disk.
- The builder may erase only a USB stick that passes Test-DzUsbDiskAllowed and that the user confirmed. Never weaken that check.
- Windows downloads must come from microsoft.com and match the catalogue size and SHA-1.
- tiny11 (builder\lib\Tiny11.psm1): the tiny11builder script is downloaded at a pinned commit and run only when its SHA-256 matches. Never copy it into this repo, never follow a branch, never add tiny11 core (it disables Windows Update and Defender).
- Never disable Windows Update or Defender; no third-party activators.
- Every tweak must be reversible (backup + DayZero.cmd -Undo); no scripts in JSON.
- winget IDs must be real (check winget-pkgs), never guessed.
- Graphics drivers (kit\lib\GpuDriver.psm1): only from the vendor's own https hosts, run only when Test-DzFileSignature confirms the vendor (NVIDIA Corporation / Advanced Micro Devices); on any failure fall back to the official page link.
- The builder is step by step: Windows steps in $script:WinSteps (Builder.ps1), Linux steps in Get-LxSteps (LinuxBuilder.ps1). A new card goes into a step page (WinStep* / LxStep* in the XAML) and the step's Errors pattern decides what blocks Next.
- Don't use "$name?" inside strings (write "${name}?").
- Linux: autoinstall.yaml must always list 'storage' in interactive-sections and never have a 'storage' key (Get-DzForbiddenAutoinstallKey). Without it Ubuntu wipes a single-disk PC by itself.
- Linux ISOs only from the https hosts in builder\linux\distros.json, and only when they match the SHA-256 published on that host. Redirects to the project's https mirrors are allowed (never http); the checksum always comes from the project's own host.
- Flathub ids must be checked (flathub GitHub org or the app's own manifest) and listed in tests\data\flatpak-ids-verified.txt, never guessed.
- Linux kit files (.sh .py .service .desktop) keep LF line endings (.gitattributes); the builder converts your scripts to LF.
- Linux builder: erase only a disk from Get-DzLinuxUsbDiskCandidate with no Problem, re-checked in Initialize-DzLinuxUsbDisk right before wipefs, and only after the user typed its name. Never add loop devices or non-USB disks to the offered list (tests replace the list instead).
- Every text dayzero.py shows (T("...") and step titles) needs a pair in kit\lang\ru.json; logs stay English.

Workflow: small change -> run the checks -> fix -> commit.